      "page_title": "Threading and the GIL",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. Definition: the GIL",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==GIL== = Global Interpreter Lock, a **mutex** inside CPython",
            "Only **one** thread runs Python bytecode at a time",
            "Protects refcounts and interpreter internals cheaply (no per-object locks)",
            "Keeps __C extensions__ simple: they can assume one thread at a time"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. Mechanism: who holds it",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Moment",
            "GIL"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "waiter times out",
              "holder asked to **drop**"
            ],
            [
              "socket recv / file read",
              "released"
            ],
            [
              "time.sleep, select/poll",
              "released"
            ],
            [
              "NumPy, hashlib, zlib",
              "C code releases"
            ],
            [
              "pure-Python loop",
              "**held**"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "import sys",
            "sys.getswitchinterval()",
            "# 0.005 s: a waiting thread",
            "# then asks the holder to",
            "# release the GIL"
          ],
          "note": "forced switches only, not a time slice"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Workload",
            "Threads help?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "I/O-bound",
              "{green:yes}, waits overlap"
            ],
            [
              "C ext, big buffers",
              "{green:yes}, GIL released"
            ],
            [
              "pure-Python CPU",
              "{red:no}, can be slower"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "CPU-bound threads only take turns, and ==contention== for the lock adds overhead. So 4 threads can run __slower__ than 1.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 3. Example: template",
