          "note": "default: min(32, os.cpu_count() + 4)"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "100 URLs",
          "text": "A serial loop waits on each response in turn. With `ex.map(fetch, urls)` the network waits **overlap**, so it's about ==N× faster== with N threads."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "stop = threading.Event()",
            "def worker():",
            "    while not stop.is_set():",
            "        do_chunk()",
            "stop.set()  # polite request"
          ],
          "note": "the thread must check the flag itself"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Threads aren't free",
          "text": "Each stack reserves virtual memory (often ==8 MB== on Linux). Thousands of threads are feasible, but it adds up. Page 5 covers asyncio, which is cheaper per task."
        }
      ],
